[issue.1850]
number = 1850
title = "[P2] Provide Docker for Autobahn before routing it to the Fly runner"
revision = "3520b1428059af90261432778c008a9ce362a0b1"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "The routing introduced by commit e0a5a9cb96428465da9d597a1a0df041a92fca04 remains at .github/workflows/paxeer-go-test.yml:187 with no runtime setup before its Make command at :201, which reaches chain.mk:526 and :530, tests/integration/autobahn/autobahn_test.go:167 and :215, and Docker build/Compose at chain.mk:283 and :436 before m.Run at tests/integration/autobahn/autobahn_test.go:172, while tools/flyci/runner/fly.toml:5 selects the Dockerless image defined at docker/flyci-runner/Dockerfile:14, tools/flyci/controller/reconcile.go:370 supplies no daemon or socket, tools/flyci/runner/entrypoint.sh:93 starts only the Actions runner, scripts/ci/runner-routing-check.sh:75 misses the indirect Make dependency, and tests/ci/test_workflow_runs_on_routed.py:34 and :110 require the incompatible routing; issue #1838 instead concerns stale literal-runner assertions at spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/input/1838.md:5."
close_comment = "Autobahn integration requires a Docker cluster, but the configurable runner image does not provide Docker. The repair will keep this job on Docker-capable hosted Ubuntu with a justified exclusion and add checks for its indirect Make and Go dependency while preserving the existing integration assertions."

